WEBVTT

00:05:57.836 --> 00:06:02.996
We spent 14 and a half days altogether,
spread over three weeks,

00:06:03.036 --> 00:06:08.876
and this was also working very long hours,
from sunrise to sunset.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.836
Whilst the team was excavating
the ichthyosaur,

00:06:12.876 --> 00:06:15.996
we also had to look out
for all sorts of other pieces

00:06:16.036 --> 00:06:18.956
in the surrounding matrix
of the ichthyosaur.

00:06:18.996 --> 00:06:20.156
So in my hand here,

00:06:20.196 --> 00:06:23.476
I'm actually holding one of the isolated
teeth from this ichthyosaur.

00:06:23.836 --> 00:06:27.636
We also found hundreds
of these squid-like ammonites,

00:06:27.676 --> 00:06:29.316
we found lots of fossil shells,

00:06:29.316 --> 00:06:30.956
and these are all really important